// Port of @angular-eslint/use-pipe-transform-interface.
//
// Implementation note: GritQL metavariables cannot bind an `implements` clause
// (`class $n implements $i { $b }` never matches), so instead of matching
// decorator+class shapes we match the @Pipe decorator and require the file to
// reference PipeTransform. This covers every class form (export, extends,
// implements-other). Known false negatives: a file that imports PipeTransform
// without implementing it, or a multi-pipe file where only one pipe implements it.
language js

`@Pipe($args)` as $dec where {
  $program <: not contains `PipeTransform`,
  register_diagnostic(span = $dec, message = "@Pipe classes must implement the PipeTransform interface.", severity = "warn")
}
